  "executive_briefing": "As of June 2026, the global tax environment is defined by the hardening of digital compliance mandates and a fragmented approach to multinational taxation. While the OECD Pillar Two framework remains the standard for large MNEs, its application is increasingly localized, moving past the initial 'hype' stage into a phase of operational implementation. Simultaneously, trade policy remains highly volatile, with the U.S. deploying aggressive tariff strategies that continue to face significant legal and judicial pushback, complicating supply chain predictability. The shift toward real-time digital tax enforcement, notably via Peppol-based e-invoicing in APAC, has transitioned from a future-looking concept to a functional necessity for compliance, signaling a broader move toward government-led 'frictionless' reporting ecosystems.",
